{
  "id": "qa-test-e",
  "name": "QA Test E — D with adaptive sizing + intermediate schemas",
  "description": "Forks from qa-test-d (pinned). Adds: (1) output schemas on all 4 intermediate test cards enforcing verdict/findings/findings_filed, (2) adaptive sizing — small artifacts route to a single qa-quick card instead of 7-card fan-out.",
  "trigger": {
    "source": "card_completed",
    "condition": {
      "assignee": "verifier",
      "status": "done",
      "metadata.verdict": "PASS",
      "title_not_prefix": "[probe]",
      "title_not_prefix2": "verify t_"
    }
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "check-merge",
      "profile": "product-owner",
      "type": "command",
      "command": "python3 ~/.hermes-teams/startup/scripts/workflow_engine/scripts/check-merge.py --board ${trigger.board}",
      "body_template": "noop — git merge check"
    },
    {
      "id": "skip",
      "profile": "product-owner",
      "type": "command",
      "command": "echo {\"status\": \"no code merge\"}",
      "body_template": "noop — skip QA"
    },
    {
      "id": "qa-receive",
      "profile": "qa",
      "skill": "live-testing",
      "body_template": "## QA Phase 0+1 — Receive, Plan, Size\n\n**Merge commit:** ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}\n**Source:** verifier card ${trigger.card_id} — ${trigger.title}\n\n**Your task:**\n1. **Receive** — read the spec/card body. Identify what was built, artifact type (CLI/API/webapp/daemon/library), scope.\n2. **Plan + Size** — extract every spec feature into testable claims. Risk-rank each P0-P4. Decide sizing: small (<10 claims, stateless), medium (10-20, stateful), large (20+, multi-service).\n\nComplete this card with metadata:\n```\n{plan_complete: true, artifact_type: \"<type>\", sizing: \"small|medium|large\",\n claims: [\"claim1\", \"claim2\", ...],\n risk_ranking: [{claim: \"...\", risk_level: \"P0|P1|P2|P3|P4\", depth: \"full|standard|smoke\"}],\n journeys: [\"journey1\", ...], exploration_targets: [\"target1\", ...]}\n```\n\nFor small artifacts: the downstream test cards will run in-session depth. For medium/large: they will use kanban fan-out or containers internally.",
      "title_template": "[qa] Plan: ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["plan_complete"],
          "properties": {
            "plan_complete": {"type": "boolean"},
            "sizing": {"type": "string", "enum": ["small", "medium", "large"]},
            "artifact_type": {"type": "string"},
            "claims": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}
          }
        }
      },
      "depends_on": ["check-merge"]
    },
    {
      "id": "qa-build",
      "profile": "qa",
      "skill": "live-testing",
      "body_template": "## QA Phase 2 — Build, containerize, smoke\n\n**Merge commit:** ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}\n**Plan:** see qa-receive card on this board\n\n**Your task:**\n1. Detect build system (package.json, Cargo.toml, pyproject.toml, go.mod, Makefile, Dockerfile).\n2. Build from source the way a user would.\n3. For medium/large artifacts: generate Containerfile if missing, build image `qa-test:<card-id>`.\n4. Smoke test: confirm artifact runs and is reachable (CLI: --help/version; server: health endpoint; webapp: URL renders).\n\nComplete this card with metadata:\n```\n{build_success: true, smoke_result: \"running|failed\"}\n```\n\nIf build fails: set build_success=false, file a Critical finding card, and block this card.",
      "title_template": "[qa] Build: ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["build_success"],
          "properties": {
            "build_success": {"type": "boolean"},
            "smoke_result": {"type": "string"}
          }
        }
      },
      "depends_on": ["qa-receive"]
    },
    {
      "id": "qa-functional",
      "profile": "qa",
      "skill": "live-testing",
      "body_template": "## QA Phase 3 — Prove claims (two-pass, DELTA-FIRST)\n\n**Merge commit:** ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}\n**Plan:** see qa-receive card for claims + risk ranking\n**Build:** see qa-build card for artifact details\n\n**CRITICAL: Test the files that CHANGED in this merge first and deepest.** Run `git diff --name-only` to identify exactly which files the merge touched. Those files get maximum edge-case depth. Unchanged sibling files get regression smoke only.\n\n**Your task:**\n1. **Pass 1 (fast):** Smoke ALL claims — happy path only. If a core claim's happy path fails, file immediately (Critical).\n2. **Pass 2 (deep):** For each claim that passed smoke, apply edge cases by risk level:\n   - P0/P1: 10+ edge cases, degradation probes, concurrent access\n   - P2: 5 edge cases, happy path journeys\n   - P3/P4: smoke only\n3. Give each claim a verdict: proven, disproven, or untested.\n\nApply universal edge cases: empty/null input, boundary values, special chars, unicode, concurrency, restart, resource exhaustion, network failure, time/date, auth.\n\nComplete this card with metadata:\n```\n{verdict: \"PASS|FAIL\",\n verdicts: [{claim_id: \"C1\", claim: \"...\", verdict: \"proven|disproven|untested\", risk_level: \"P0|P1|P2|P3|P4\", evidence: \"command + exit code\"}],\n findings: [{severity: \"Critical|Important|Minor|Note\", claim: \"...\", detail: \"...\", reproduction: \"copy-pasteable commands\"}],\n findings_filed: <count of kanban cards actually created for findings>}\n```\n\nIf you report findings_filed > 0, each finding MUST have a corresponding kanban card created on this board.",
      "title_template": "[qa] Functional: ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["verdict"],
          "properties": {
            "verdict": {"type": "string", "enum": ["PASS", "FAIL"]},
            "findings": {"type": "array"},
            "findings_filed": {"type": "integer"}
          }
        }
      },
      "depends_on": ["qa-receive", "qa-build"]
    },
    {
      "id": "qa-journeys",
      "profile": "qa",
      "skill": "live-testing",
      "body_template": "## QA Phase 4 — Walk user journeys\n\n**Merge commit:** ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}\n**Plan:** see qa-receive card for journeys list\n**Build:** see qa-build card for artifact details\n\n**Your task:**\nExecute each journey from the plan as a real user: click through UI, call API sequence, pipe CLI commands. Give each journey a verdict.\n\nA journey that can't be completed gets disproven even if every component claim passed — the broken flow itself is the finding.\n\nComplete this card with metadata:\n```\n{verdict: \"PASS|FAIL\",\n journey_verdicts: [{journey: \"...\", verdict: \"proven|disproven\", evidence: \"command chain or screenshot ref\"}],\n findings: [{severity: \"...\", claim: \"...\", detail: \"...\", reproduction: \"...\"}],\n findings_filed: <count>}\n```",
      "title_template": "[qa] Journeys: ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["verdict"],
          "properties": {
            "verdict": {"type": "string", "enum": ["PASS", "FAIL"]},
            "findings": {"type": "array"},
            "findings_filed": {"type": "integer"}
          }
        }
      },
      "depends_on": ["qa-receive", "qa-build"]
    },
    {
      "id": "qa-security",
      "profile": "qa",
      "skill": "live-testing",
      "body_template": "## QA Phase 5 — Non-functional + security depth\n\n**Merge commit:** ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}\n**Build:** see qa-build card for artifact details\n\n**Your task:**\nRun the cheap, fast checks that catch regressions functional tests miss:\n\n**Security smoke:** IDOR, auth bypass, secrets in output, dependency scan\n**Security depth:** CSRF, XSS, SSRF, open redirect, path traversal, command injection, session fixation\n**Performance:** response time, 30s smoke load, degradation under concurrency\n**Accessibility** (webapps only): axe-core scan, tab-order, contrast\n**Expanded edge cases:** data integrity, idempotency, cache invalidation, graceful shutdown, connection pool exhaustion, locale/i18n, Unicode normalization, API versioning, pagination drift, rate limiting, WebSocket reconnection, upgrade/migration, recovery\n\nComplete this card with metadata:\n```\n{verdict: \"PASS|FAIL\",\n checks: [{check: \"...\", result: \"pass|fail|skip\", reason: \"...\"}],\n findings: [{severity: \"...\", claim: \"...\", detail: \"...\", reproduction: \"...\"}],\n findings_filed: <count>}\n```",
      "title_template": "[qa] Security: ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["verdict"],
          "properties": {
            "verdict": {"type": "string", "enum": ["PASS", "FAIL"]},
            "findings": {"type": "array"},
            "findings_filed": {"type": "integer"}
          }
        }
      },
      "depends_on": ["qa-receive", "qa-build"]
    },
    {
      "id": "qa-explore",
      "profile": "qa",
      "skill": "live-testing",
      "body_template": "## QA Phase 6 — Explore beyond the spec\n\n**Merge commit:** ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}\n**Plan:** see qa-receive card for exploration targets\n**Build:** see qa-build card for artifact details\n\n**Your task:**\nFind what the spec DIDN'T anticipate — bugs in the gaps between features.\n\nFor each exploration target, write a charter (one-sentence mission):\n- \"Probe the file-upload feature for size, type, and encoding edge handling\"\n- \"Probe the auth flow for token expiry, refresh, and concurrent session behavior\"\n\nTest **graceful degradation**: kill the DB, make upstream return 500, fill the disk. Test **recovery**: crash the process, restart, verify state intact.\n\nComplete this card with metadata:\n```\n{verdict: \"PASS|FAIL\",\n charters: [{charter: \"...\", result: \"clean|bugs_found\", findings: \"...\"}],\n findings: [{severity: \"...\", claim: \"...\", detail: \"...\", reproduction: \"...\"}],\n findings_filed: <count>}\n```",
      "title_template": "[qa] Explore: ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["verdict"],
          "properties": {
            "verdict": {"type": "string", "enum": ["PASS", "FAIL"]},
            "findings": {"type": "array"},
            "findings_filed": {"type": "integer"}
          }
        }
      },
      "depends_on": ["qa-receive", "qa-build"]
    },
    {
      "id": "qa-quick",
      "profile": "qa",
      "skill": "live-testing",
      "body_template": "## QA Quick re-test — small artifact, single session\n\n**Merge commit:** ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}\n**Plan:** see qa-receive card for claims + sizing\n\nYou are the last gate for a SMALL artifact (<10 claims, stateless). Run your full live-testing protocol in a single session — no fan-out needed:\n\n1. Build + smoke\n2. Two-pass claims (smoke all, deep test passing)\n3. Quick journeys\n4. Security smoke (IDOR, secrets, deps)\n5. Quick exploration\n6. Verdict\n\n**CRITICAL: Test the files that CHANGED first.** Run `git diff --name-only` to identify the delta.\n\nFile findings as kanban cards (Critical → block, others → ship).\n\n**Completion metadata contract:**\n- PASS: metadata={verdict: \"PASS\", findings_count: 0, findings: [], commit_tested: \"<sha>\", findings_filed: 0}\n- FAIL: metadata={verdict: \"FAIL\", findings_count: N, findings: [{severity, claim, detail, reproduction}], commit_tested: \"<sha>\", findings_filed: N}",
      "title_template": "[qa] Quick: ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["verdict", "findings_count", "commit_tested"],
          "properties": {
            "verdict": {"type": "string", "enum": ["PASS", "FAIL"]},
            "findings_count": {"type": "integer"},
            "findings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object"}},
            "commit_tested": {"type": "string"},
            "findings_filed": {"type": "integer"}
          }
        }
      },
      "depends_on": ["qa-receive"]
    },
    {
      "id": "qa-verdict",
      "profile": "qa",
      "skill": "live-testing",
      "body_template": "## QA Phase 7 — Verdict + report\n\n**Merge commit:** ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}\n\n**Your task:**\nSynthesize results from all 4 test cards on this board:\n- qa-functional: claim verdicts + findings\n- qa-journeys: journey verdicts + findings\n- qa-security: security check results + findings\n- qa-explore: exploration findings\n\nRead each card's completion via `kanban_show`. Do NOT re-test — synthesize.\n\n**For each phase, cite ONE key piece of evidence inline** (the most important command result, exit code, or finding from that phase's card). This makes the verdict self-contained — a reader shouldn't need to open child cards for the headline evidence.\n\n**Decision logic:**\n- Any Critical finding → file findings as kanban cards (bug→debugger, non-bug→tech-lead), then complete with verdict=FAIL\n- Only Important/Minor/Note → file findings, complete with verdict=PASS (ship with follow-ups)\n- All proven, no findings → verdict=PASS\n\nInclude testability feedback (design decisions that made testing hard).\n\n**Completion metadata contract:**\n- PASS: metadata={verdict: \"PASS\", findings_count: 0, findings: [], commit_tested: \"<sha>\", findings_filed: 0}\n- FAIL: metadata={verdict: \"FAIL\", findings_count: N, findings: [{severity, claim, detail, reproduction}], commit_tested: \"<sha>\", findings_filed: N}",
      "title_template": "[qa] Verdict: ${nodes.check-merge.output.commit_sha}",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["verdict", "findings_count", "commit_tested"],
          "properties": {
            "verdict": {"type": "string", "enum": ["PASS", "FAIL"]},
            "findings_count": {"type": "integer"},
            "findings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object"}},
            "commit_tested": {"type": "string"},
            "findings_filed": {"type": "integer"}
          }
        }
      },
      "depends_on": ["qa-functional", "qa-journeys", "qa-security", "qa-explore"]
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {"from": "check-merge", "to": "qa-receive", "condition": "${nodes.check-merge.output.should_test} == 'true'"},
    {"from": "check-merge", "to": "skip", "condition": "${nodes.check-merge.output.should_test} != 'true'"},
    {"from": "qa-receive", "to": "qa-build", "condition": "${nodes.qa-receive.output.sizing} != 'small'"},
    {"from": "qa-receive", "to": "qa-quick", "condition": "${nodes.qa-receive.output.sizing} == 'small'"},
    {"from": "qa-build", "to": "qa-functional"},
    {"from": "qa-build", "to": "qa-journeys"},
    {"from": "qa-build", "to": "qa-security"},
    {"from": "qa-build", "to": "qa-explore"},
    {"from": "qa-functional", "to": "qa-verdict"},
    {"from": "qa-journeys", "to": "qa-verdict"},
    {"from": "qa-security", "to": "qa-verdict"},
    {"from": "qa-explore", "to": "qa-verdict"}
  ]
}
